y heroic monkeys advanced towards the son of Ravana.","alignment":{"type":"approximate","confidence":0.22,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-81-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6068012","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a533fc002d4202006d431a6f32be187c046f6bcfddf862aad60529c31cdec69d","compact":"de3507a809edb72310a2f5e30d473fff0099ff7b11b32562373f7db730601b97","nasal":"06cef320d31d3a201bab974a05312ac54a25b494f08dfe8ddc96ed67fac374b7"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-68-13","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":68,"verse":13,"english":"Seeing her on the car, innocent, poor, deprived of joy and brought under the influence of the son of the lord Rākşasas that great monkey thought within himself— 'What must be the intention of Indrajit?' and accompanied by heroic monkeys advanced towards the son of Ravana.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-81-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6068013","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7db0cf1e8340693b6b5a44f4103d0b195fc576c4252a39cb8a56573ca8b5456d","compact":"1340797e8b19ec30dacd56cde5f38631014c3707a66ed0fc3d09b34e390ff88c","nasal":"d8af6da4a8951445fc95de1a4dd4e22d8674d90fcb97fd731cf8866984c21e45"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-68-14","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":68,"verse":14,"english":"Beholding that monkey host, Ravana's son became beside himself with ire and unsheathing his weapon Nistrinsha, caught her by the hair.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.662,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-81-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6068014","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f88fb418362b817fe7a5c401497735efef23ca0022a90ab499646128fdecda32","compact":"8d781bcbcc3035cb27b96875237dc23996284af9aac