le! O wicked! O! cruel and dishonourable wight! O you having vice for your prowess!","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.51,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-81-17","DUTT-6-81-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6068017","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3cfc0feb86edb6c3f780f76b37cd2754c35bd805a7a3894ac169b37a60d96219","compact":"1b833a3480c1443e3309738b26802cc065dec7b353bd5a2e107dfa57893dbf0c","nasal":"1000c6dfe5e7b512468ae1f18563544d88c71bfd14f8a19dcd502da4f0361a17"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-68-18","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":68,"verse":18,"english":"O! cursed are you, since you have cherished such a desire and engaged in such a vicious deed. O vile! O wicked! O! cruel and dishonourable wight! O you having vice for your prowess!","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.925,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-81-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6068018","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e5e837557667f6d07f7c66d5ae71c0be4be9126a218b51933e903c223c3c3909","compact":"f77182d946b72feedafb7ac3a8f856bbceac4ae29a0546db5de169bb9729864b","nasal":"f77182d946b72feedafb7ac3a8f856bbceac4ae29a0546db5de169bb9729864b"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-68-19","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":68,"verse":19,"english":"O shameless! Are you not ashamed of perpetrating such an inhuman deed. What has Maithili done by you, O cruel one! that you are ready to slay her—She has been banished from her home, territory and has been separated from her lord.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.836,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-81-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6068019","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"aa32affe93c8b6d122a40f9edae8382859286b05390bcd14d87fa2fa532cd3f3","compac